# Surf Life Saving Australia (SLSA)

National peak body for surf lifesaving in Australia. Federated 199,000-member, ~$100M, ~315-club organisation. Top of the hierarchy: SLSA → State → Region → Area → Club.

## Nick's relationships

Two distinct threads:

1. **SLSA Deputy Chair** — separate volunteer governance role. Delivered the board-endorsed national water safety supervision policy (adopted as a national standard).
2. **LIMSOC National Scaling Strategy** — paid independent consulting engagement through Nicholas Wood Digital Consulting. Scope: national IMS architecture, feature briefs, delivery workflow, season priorities. Status: completed 2026, now the lead case study for the consulting pivot.

## Workspace

Primary project home: `workspace/limsoc-national-ims/`. Artefacts (discovery feedback, season priorities, IMS scenarios) under `limsoc-national-ims/artifacts/`.

## Distinction worth keeping straight

The SLSA consulting engagement (national) is separate from the LSV volunteer SLCO role (state). The two often touch the same LIMSOC subject matter but have different governance, contracts, and decision rights.
